# Normalise to LF in the repository, check out with the platform's native
# endings. core.autocrlf is already true on this machine, so this changes
# nothing today — it makes the behaviour a property of the repository rather
# than of whoever happened to clone it.
* text=auto

# Files executed on Linux no matter where they were edited, so they must keep
# LF in the working tree as well as in the repository.
#
# provision-vps.sh is the one that bites: it is scp'd to the VPS and run by bash
# there. Under `text=auto` alone a Windows checkout gives it CRLF, and bash
# fails on the first line with $'\r': command not found — before the script has
# done anything, and with an error that names neither the file nor the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Regenerated rather than merged, and ignored — see .gitignore. The driver named
# here exists only in local git config.
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify
